ity against a random hand. To call (limp), I need to contribute 50 chips into a pot that will be 200 total (100 from BB + 50 my post + 50 my call), offering 3:1 pot odds. I only need 25% equity to make this call profitable. Since 48% > 25%, and I will have the advantage of position post-flop (acting last on the Flop, Turn, River), calling is statistically +EV. Raising would bloat the pot with a weak hand, and folding would forfeit the equity for no reason. Thus, checking/calling is the optimal move to see a flop cheaply.\n\nReason: The hand Q2o has sufficient equity (~48%) to justify a call given the 3:1 pot odds and positional advantage in a heads-up match. Raising is too risky with this holding, and folding is too tight.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
